From: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: r8125: boot option to skip the shutdown hook on a reboot

A/B knob for the warm-reboot NIC link-training failure. Keeping PERST#
released on reboot (post/0005) did not help, so the next suspect is the
state this driver leaves in the NIC on its way down. The NIC keeps power
through a warm reset, so that state can reach the firmware.

"r8125.reboot_shutdown=0" skips rtl8125_shutdown() on SYSTEM_RESTART.
The default (1) keeps the old behaviour. Power-off is not affected.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8125/r8125_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8125/r8125_n.c
@@ -312,6 +312,11 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(aspm, "Enable ASPM.");
 module_param(s5wol, int, 0);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(s5wol, "Enable Shutdown Wake On Lan.");
 
+/* A/B knob for warm-reboot link-training tests: 0 skips the shutdown hook on a reboot. */
+static int reboot_shutdown = 1;
+module_param(reboot_shutdown, int, 0);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(reboot_shutdown, "Run the shutdown hook on a reboot (default 1).");
+
 module_param(s5_keep_curr_mac, int, 0);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(s5_keep_curr_mac, "Enable Shutdown Keep Current MAC Address.");
 
@@ -21078,6 +21083,11 @@ static void rtl8125_shutdown(struct pci_dev *pdev)
         struct net_device *dev = pci_get_drvdata(pdev);
         struct rtl8125_private *tp = netdev_priv(dev);
 
+        if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART && !reboot_shutdown) {
+                dev_info(&pdev->dev, "reboot: shutdown hook skipped\n");
+                return;
+        }
+
         rtnl_lock();
 
         if (HW_DASH_SUPPORT_DASH(tp))
